<%- include('partials/inner_header') %>

<div class="container">
    <div class="calculator-container">
        <h1 class="calculator-title"><%= title %></h1>
<%- include('partials/ad_unit') %>

        <div class="unit-switcher">
            <button id="metricBtn" class="unit-btn active">Metric (kg, cm)</button>
            <button id="imperialBtn" class="unit-btn">Imperial (lbs, ft, in)</button>
        </div>

        <div class="calculator-grid">
            <div class="form-section">
                <form id="ketoForm">
                    <!-- Metric Units -->
                    <div id="metricInputs">
                        <div class="form-group">
                            <label for="weightKg">Weight (kg)</label>
                            <div class="input-wrapper"><input type="number" id="weightKg" step="0.1" placeholder="e.g., 80"></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="form-group">
                            <label for="heightCm">Height (cm)</label>
                            <div class="input-wrapper"><input type="number" id="heightCm" step="1" placeholder="e.g., 175"></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Imperial Units -->
                    <div id="imperialInputs" style="display: none;">
                        <div class="form-group">
                            <label for="weightLbs">Weight (lbs)</label>
                            <div class="input-wrapper"><input type="number" id="weightLbs" step="0.1" placeholder="e.g., 176"></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="form-group">
                            <label>Height (ft, in)</label>
                            <div class="height-imperial-inputs">
                                <div class="input-wrapper"><input type="number" id="heightFt" placeholder="e.g., 5"><span class="input-adornment">ft</span></div>
                                <div class="input-wrapper"><input type="number" id="heightIn" placeholder="e.g., 9"><span class="input-adornment">in</span></div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="form-group">
                        <label for="age">Age (years)</label>
                        <div class="input-wrapper"><input type="number" id="age" step="1" placeholder="e.g., 30"></div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="form-group">
                        <label for="gender">Gender</label>
                        <div class="input-wrapper">
                            <select id="gender">
                                <option value="male">Male</option>
                                <option value="female">Female</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="form-group">
                        <label for="activityLevel">Activity Level</label>
                        <div class="input-wrapper">
                            <select id="activityLevel">
                                <option value="1.2">Sedentary (little or no exercise)</option>
                                <option value="1.375">Lightly Active (1–3 days/week)</option>
                                <option value="1.55">Moderately Active (3–5 days/week)</option>
                                <option value="1.725">Very Active (6–7 days/week)</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="form-group">
                        <label for="goal">Goal</label>
                        <div class="input-wrapper">
                            <select id="goal">
                                <option value="lose">Lose Weight (-20% calories)</option>
                                <option value="maintain" selected>Maintain Weight</option>
                                <option value="gain">Gain Muscle (+10% calories)</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="form-group">
                        <label for="bodyFat">Body Fat % <span style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--text-muted);">(optional)</span></label>
                        <div class="input-wrapper"><input type="number" id="bodyFat" step="0.5" min="1" max="70" placeholder="e.g., 20 (leave blank to skip)"></div>
                    </div>
                </form>
            </div>

            <div class="result-section" id="result-section">
                <div class="placeholder">Enter your details to calculate your keto macros.</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-section">
            <div class="accordion-item"><button class="accordion-header"><span>What is the ketogenic diet?</span><span class="icon">+</span></button><div class="accordion-content"><p>The ketogenic (keto) diet is a very low-carbohydrate, high-fat diet. By drastically reducing carbohydrate intake and replacing it with fat, your body enters a metabolic state called ketosis — where it becomes highly efficient at burning fat for energy instead of glucose. It also turns fat into ketones in the liver, which can supply energy for the brain.</p></div></div>
            <div class="accordion-item"><button class="accordion-header"><span>How many carbs can I eat on keto?</span><span class="icon">+</span></button><div class="accordion-content"><p>Most people need to stay under 20–50g of net carbs per day to enter and maintain ketosis. Net carbs = total carbs minus fiber. Most people successfully enter ketosis below 25g of net carbs. Individual carb tolerance varies, so some people may need to stay even lower.</p></div></div>
            <div class="accordion-item"><button class="accordion-header"><span>What foods are keto-friendly?</span><span class="icon">+</span></button><div class="accordion-content"><p>Keto-friendly foods include:</p><ul><li><strong>Proteins:</strong> Meat, poultry, fish, seafood, eggs</li><li><strong>Dairy:</strong> Cheese, butter, heavy cream, Greek yogurt (in moderation)</li><li><strong>Fats:</strong> Avocado, olive oil, coconut oil, nuts and seeds</li><li><strong>Vegetables:</strong> Leafy greens, broccoli, cauliflower, zucchini, peppers</li></ul><p>Avoid: bread, pasta, rice, sugar, most fruits, and starchy vegetables.</p></div></div>
        </div>

<%- include('partials/ad_unit') %>

        <div style="margin-top:2rem;padding:1.5rem;background:var(--card-bg);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border-color);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 1rem;font-size:1rem;color:var(--text-muted);">🔗 Related Calculators</h3>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.5rem;">
                <a href="/macro-calculator" style="padding:0.4rem 0.9rem;background:var(--accent-gradient);color:#fff;border-radius:20px;font-size:0.85rem;text-decoration:none;">🥦 Macro Calculator</a>
                <a href="/calorie-calculator" style="padding:0.4rem 0.9rem;background:var(--accent-gradient);color:#fff;border-radius:20px;font-size:0.85rem;text-decoration:none;">🍽️ Calorie Calculator</a>
                <a href="/tdee-calculator" style="padding:0.4rem 0.9rem;background:var(--accent-gradient);color:#fff;border-radius:20px;font-size:0.85rem;text-decoration:none;">⚡ TDEE Calculator</a>
                <a href="/protein-intake-calculator" style="padding:0.4rem 0.9rem;background:var(--accent-gradient);color:#fff;border-radius:20px;font-size:0.85rem;text-decoration:none;">🥩 Protein Intake</a>
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>
</div>

<script>
    let currentUnit = 'metric';
    const resultDiv = document.getElementById('result-section');
    const metricBtn = document.getElementById('metricBtn');
    const imperialBtn = document.getElementById('imperialBtn');
    const metricInputsDiv = document.getElementById('metricInputs');
    const imperialInputsDiv = document.getElementById('imperialInputs');

    function switchUnit(unit) {
        currentUnit = unit;
        metricBtn.classList.toggle('active', unit === 'metric');
        imperialBtn.classList.toggle('active', unit === 'imperial');
        metricInputsDiv.style.display = unit === 'metric' ? 'block' : 'none';
        imperialInputsDiv.style.display = unit === 'imperial' ? 'block' : 'none';
        document.querySelectorAll('input').forEach(i => i.value = '');
        resultDiv.innerHTML = `<div class="placeholder">Enter your details to calculate your keto macros.</div>`;
    }
    metricBtn.addEventListener('click', () => switchUnit('metric'));
    imperialBtn.addEventListener('click', () => switchUnit('imperial'));

    document.querySelectorAll('input, select').forEach(el => {
        el.addEventListener('input', calculateKeto);
        el.addEventListener('change', calculateKeto);
    });

    function calculateKeto() {
        let weightInKg, heightInCm;
        if (currentUnit === 'metric') {
            weightInKg = parseFloat(document.getElementById('weightKg').value);
            heightInCm = parseFloat(document.getElementById('heightCm').value);
        } else {
            const lbs = parseFloat(document.getElementById('weightLbs').value);
            const ft = parseFloat(document.getElementById('heightFt').value);
            const inches = parseFloat(document.getElementById('heightIn').value) || 0;
            if (!isNaN(lbs)) weightInKg = lbs * 0.453592;
            if (!isNaN(ft)) heightInCm = (ft * 12 + inches) * 2.54;
        }

        const age = parseFloat(document.getElementById('age').value);
        const gender = document.getElementById('gender').value;
        const activityMultiplier = parseFloat(document.getElementById('activityLevel').value);
        const goal = document.getElementById('goal').value;
        const bodyFatPct = parseFloat(document.getElementById('bodyFat').value);

        if (isNaN(weightInKg) || isNaN(heightInCm) || isNaN(age) || weightInKg <= 0 || heightInCm <= 0 || age <= 0) {
            resultDiv.innerHTML = `<div class="placeholder">Please fill in all required fields.</div>`;
            return;
        }

        // Mifflin-St Jeor BMR
        let bmr;
        if (gender === 'male') {
            bmr = (10 * weightInKg) + (6.25 * heightInCm) - (5 * age) + 5;
        } else {
            bmr = (10 * weightInKg) + (6.25 * heightInCm) - (5 * age) - 161;
        }

        let tdee = bmr * activityMultiplier;

        // Goal adjustment
        let goalMultiplier = 1;
        if (goal === 'lose') goalMultiplier = 0.80;
        else if (goal === 'gain') goalMultiplier = 1.10;
        const dailyCalories = Math.round(tdee * goalMultiplier);

        // Keto macro split: Fat 70%, Protein 25%, Carbs 5%
        // But protein minimum = 1.6g/kg bodyweight
        const netCarbs = 22; // ~22g net carbs (within 20-25g range)
        const carbCalories = netCarbs * 4;

        let proteinG = Math.max(
            Math.round((dailyCalories * 0.25) / 4),
            Math.round(weightInKg * 1.6)
        );
        const proteinCalories = proteinG * 4;
        const fatCalories = dailyCalories - carbCalories - proteinCalories;
        const fatG = Math.round(fatCalories / 9);

        // Macro percentages for chart
        const totalCals = proteinCalories + fatCalories + carbCalories;
        const fatPct = Math.round((fatCalories / totalCals) * 100);
        const proteinPct = Math.round((proteinCalories / totalCals) * 100);
        const carbPct = 100 - fatPct - proteinPct;

        const bodyFatNote = !isNaN(bodyFatPct) && bodyFatPct > 0
            ? `<p class="result-sub-text">💪 Lean Body Mass: <strong>${(weightInKg * (1 - bodyFatPct / 100)).toFixed(1)} kg</strong></p>`
            : '';

        resultDiv.innerHTML = `
            <div class="result-display-new">
                <p class="result-main-text">Daily Calories: <strong>${dailyCalories.toLocaleString()} kcal</strong></p>
                <hr class="result-divider" />
                <p class="result-sub-text">🥩 Protein: <strong>${proteinG}g</strong> (${proteinPct}%)</p>
                <p class="result-sub-text">🧈 Fat: <strong>${fatG}g</strong> (${fatPct}%)</p>
                <p class="result-sub-text">🌿 Net Carbs: <strong>${netCarbs}g</strong> (${carbPct}%)</p>
                ${bodyFatNote}
                <hr class="result-divider" />
                <p class="result-sub-text" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;font-weight:600;">Macro Distribution</p>
                <div style="display:flex;height:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;width:100%;">
                    <div style="width:${fatPct}%;background:#f59e0b;" title="Fat ${fatPct}%"></div>
                    <div style="width:${proteinPct}%;background:#6366f1;" title="Protein ${proteinPct}%"></div>
                    <div style="width:${carbPct}%;background:#10b981;" title="Carbs ${carbPct}%"></div>
                </div>
                <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;margin-top:0.4rem;font-size:0.78rem;color:var(--text-muted);">
                    <span><span style="display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;background:#f59e0b;border-radius:2px;margin-right:3px;"></span>Fat</span>
                    <span><span style="display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;background:#6366f1;border-radius:2px;margin-right:3px;"></span>Protein</span>
                    <span><span style="display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;background:#10b981;border-radius:2px;margin-right:3px;"></span>Carbs</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        `;
    }

    document.querySelectorAll('.accordion-header').forEach(header => {
        header.addEventListener('click', () => {
            const accordionItem = header.parentElement;
            accordionItem.classList.toggle('active');
            const content = header.nextElementSibling;
            content.style.maxHeight = accordionItem.classList.contains('active') ? content.scrollHeight + 'px' : '0px';
        });
    });
</script>

<%- include('partials/inner_footer') %>
